\title{NOTES-M2 - family EV: EVAL, FORCE, APPLY, INST, ARGV, DOM (owner: M2)}
\taxon{Report}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{machine}
\tag{performance}
\meta{origin}{rlvm-machine/NOTES-M2.md}
\meta{moved}{2026-11-24}
\import{base-macros}

\p{File: \code{\verb~|src/main/java/rlvm/machine/Eval.java~}. Tests: \code{\verb~|M2EvalTest~} (rows of ISA 4.2 / 4.3.1, fast), \code{\verb~|M2EquivTest~} (convention and inert-loop equivalence, fast), \code{\verb~|M2DeepTest~} (stack safety; the full sizes are group \code{\verb~|slow~}), helper \code{\verb~|M2~}. Spec: ISA 4.2, 4.3 (FORCE, APPLY, INST), 4.3.1, 4.4.3 (DOM), 2.4, 2.6, 3.1, 5.1-5.2; convention H1-H12.}

\subtree{
\title{1. What a caller must know}

\table{
\tr{\th{Point}\th{Rule}}
\tr{\td{A result may be a suspension}\td{\code{\verb~|EVAL~}, \code{\verb~|APPLY~}, \code{\verb~|INST~} return a value \strong{or a SUSP}: a delayed argument that the term passes on (a variable bound to a suspension, a field taken out of a constructor application, a let variable). Call \code{\verb~|FORCE~} where the value is needed. \code{\verb~|DOM~} always returns a forced value. \code{\verb~|FORCE~} never returns a SUSP}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|VAL~} is never a SUSP}\td{ISA 2.6. \code{\verb~|FORCE~} forces the result of its \code{\verb~|EVAL~} again if that is a suspension; a tabled \code{\verb~|EVAL~} whose result is still a suspension after \code{\verb~|PEEK~} is \strong{not tabled} (D1)}}
\tr{\td{Variables are \code{\verb~|PEEK~}ed}\td{\code{\verb~|EVAL~} / \code{\verb~|ARGV~} of a variable is \code{\verb~|PEEK(GET)~}: a plain suspension whose value is known is replaced by the value before it enters a spine or a register; a LET suspension is kept (ISA 2.1, 2.8) (D8)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|let~}}\td{A \code{\verb~|let~} inside an evaluated term is zeta by sharing with \strong{plain} values (D9). Only INFER makes LET suspensions (the let variable of \code{\verb~|infer_let~}); \code{\verb~|EVAL~} keeps one when it reads it through a variable, and what is built from it is OPEN}}
\tr{\td{HOLE}\td{An argument of \code{\verb~|APPLY~} / \code{\verb~|INST~} may be HOLE iff the binder is not read. \code{\verb~|APPLY~} raises \code{\verb~|fault(E_HOLE)~} if a HOLE argument would enter a spine (\code{\verb~|MKAPP~}); reading HOLE through a variable is \code{\verb~|fault(E_HOLE)~} (in \code{\verb~|Runs.get~})}}
\tr{\td{Scratch and environments}\td{\code{\verb~|APPLY(f, xb, n)~} reads \code{\verb~|X[xb .. xb + n)~} and leaves it to the caller. Every judgment restores \code{\verb~|xp~} and \code{\verb~|ep~} when it returns a result; the saved \code{\verb~|ep~} / \code{\verb~|xb~} are payload words of its frames (H7)}}
\tr{\td{Inert nests}\td{The evaluation of an inert application that \code{\verb~|ARGV~} performs at once (constant head, or a variable head bound to a neutral) is an iteration of the inert-nest loop of the enclosing \code{\verb~|EVAL~}: \strong{one tick per application node, no call event}. A whole nest of constant-headed applications is therefore one \code{\verb~|EVAL~} call event. \code{\verb~|SW_INERT_LOOP~} no longer selects anything (D12)}}
\tr{\td{Ticks}\td{One per \code{\verb~|EVAL~} of an application, let or projection node that is not a memo hit (inert nodes included); one per \code{\verb~|FORCE~} of a pending suspension, per \code{\verb~|APPLY~} of a closure or pending suspension, per \code{\verb~|INST~} without \code{\verb~|COD~}, per \code{\verb~|DOM~} without \code{\verb~|M_DOM~}. Leaves, closures, \code{\verb~|MKAPP~} of a neutral, \code{\verb~|MKSUSP~} and memo hits are free}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Eval.Ext~} (\code{\verb~|m.x2~})}\td{\code{\verb~|body~}, \code{\verb~|en~}, \code{\verb~|amOpen~}: second results of helpers (like \code{\verb~|m.envBase~}); \code{\verb~|ownFirst~} (gated tabling); \code{\verb~|cm~} (closed-term memo), \code{\verb~|am~} (APPLY memo) with its governor \code{\verb~|amWin~}, \code{\verb~|amWinHits~}, \code{\verb~|amOff~}; \code{\verb~|xsw~}, \code{\verb~|depthK~} (measurement bits, section 6); statistics \code{\verb~|hits~}, \code{\verb~|lazy~}, \code{\verb~|amHits~} (only with \code{\verb~|m.stats~})}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Eval.evalBody~}}\td{For a caller that binds the arguments of a binder body itself (M5's \code{\verb~|TWALK~} in telescope mode): \code{\verb~|EVAL~} of a term entered like the body of a beta step: without a tabling record under \code{\verb~|SW_M2A~} (D19), else \code{\verb~|Eval.eval~}}}
\tr{\td{Switches of this package}\td{\code{\verb~|SW_GATED_TABLING~} (\code{\verb~|gated~}): tabling by node flags, with the depth rule (D14, D21). \code{\verb~|SW_M2A~} (\code{\verb~|m2a~}): bodies without a tabling record, projection selector (D19, D22). \code{\verb~|SW_M2B~} (\code{\verb~|m2b~}): the APPLY memo (D23). Without a switch, changing no result: the closed-term memo (D20), the argument picker (D22). Section 6}}
\tr{\td{Debug hooks (ISA 5.5)}\td{scopeaudit is in \code{\verb~|Runs.get~} (M1), which every variable read of this family goes through; maskaudit before every \code{\verb~|PRUNE~} made here (closures, suspensions, tabling records), sharecheck when the walk enters an untabled node (gated tabling), memocheck on \code{\verb~|VAL~}, \code{\verb~|COD~}, \code{\verb~|M_DOM~} (D16)}}
}

\p{Frames (the payload is the parameter list of the continuation step):}

\pre{\verb~|
EVAL[0](t, eb, en, ls)                   the entry step (spilled)
EVAL[NB](t, eb, en, ls)                  the entry step of a body evaluated without a tabling record (SW_M2A), spilled
EVAL[IN](t, lo, u, eb, en, ls)           an inert application met by ARGV, beyond the depth bound (no call event);
                                         lo = first id of the parent's export segment (-1: a root), u = depth in the nest
EVAL[HEAD](s, xb, n, eb, en, ls)         waits for the value of the head          s = tabling record, or -t (t is not
                                         tabled); X[xb - 1] = the depth of the node in its inert nest
EVAL[HEADF](s, xb, n, eb, en, ls)        waits for the forced head
EVAL[ARG](s, f, xb, n, i, eb, en, ls)    waits for argument i (an inert application); f = the forced head
EVAL[APP](s, xb)                         waits for APPLY
EVAL[BODY](s, ep0)                       waits for the body of a let chain
EVAL[PROJ](t, s)                         waits for the struct of a projection
EVAL[LET](t, s, eb, en, ls, ep0)         waits for the value bound by let node t (an inert application)
FORCE[0](s)   FORCE[1](s, ep0)   FORCE[2](s)
APPLY[0](f, xb, n)   APPLY[1](xb, n, k)   APPLY[2](xb, n, k, ep0)          k = arguments consumed
APPLY[3](xb, n, k, ep0, g, j)                                               as APPLY[2]; the step applied closure g to j
                                                                            arguments and is recorded in the APPLY memo (SW_M2B)
INST[0](pi, x)   INST[1](memo, ep0)   INST[2](memo, xb)                     memo = the record whose COD is written, or 0;
                                                                            INST[2]: the closure's block (SW_CODE)
DOM[0](v)   DOM[1](v, ep0)   DOM[2](v)
ARGV[0](t, eb, en, ls)                   never written (D7)
~}
}

\subtree{
\title{2. Deviations from ISA.md, with the reason}

\table{
\tr{\th{\verb~|#~}\th{Where}\th{Deviation}\th{Reason}}
\tr{\td{D1}\td{4.2 \code{\verb~|tabled(t)~}: "\code{\verb~|VAL(s) = result~}"}\td{The result is \code{\verb~|PEEK~}ed; if it is still a SUSP (pending, or a LET suspension) it is returned and \strong{not} stored. Evaluating the node again redoes one level; its sub-terms are tabled}\td{ISA 2.6: \code{\verb~|VAL~} is never a SUSP, and \code{\verb~|PEEK~} / \code{\verb~|forceFast~} / every consumer rely on that. Forcing instead would make \code{\verb~|EVAL~} strict where the ISA and the official \code{\verb~|instantiate~} are lazy}}
\tr{\td{D2}\td{4.3 \code{\verb~|FORCE~}: "\code{\verb~|call EVAL(term, frame, ls)~}, \code{\verb~|VAL <- A~}"}\td{\code{\verb~|VAL <- FORCE(A)~}: the result of the \code{\verb~|EVAL~} is forced again while it is a suspension (frame \code{\verb~|FORCE[2]~})}\td{same invariant; \code{\verb~|(fun x => x) a~} with an active \code{\verb~|a~} evaluates to the suspension of \code{\verb~|a~}}}
\tr{\td{D3}\td{4.3 \code{\verb~|FORCE~}}\td{A plain suspension is evaluated by \code{\verb~|evalAt~}, the \code{\verb~|EVAL~} judgment without the tabling probe: the suspension \em{is} the tabling record of its term. A LET suspension is a record of its own (M1: aux 1) and goes through \code{\verb~|eval~}, so the plain record is tabled as usual}\td{saves \code{\verb~|PRUNE~} + one probe per \code{\verb~|FORCE~}; same call events (\code{\verb~|FORCE~}, \code{\verb~|EVAL~}), same ticks}}
\tr{\td{D4}\td{4.4.3 / 2.6 \code{\verb~|DOM~}: "memo m1, else call \code{\verb~|EVAL(domain term, frame, ls)~}"}\td{\code{\verb~|DOM~} forces the value of the domain term; \code{\verb~|M_DOM~} never holds a suspension}\td{the domain is the type of the variable \code{\verb~|OPEN~} picks (2.8) and is compared at once by every caller; a memo word should hold a value. A top-level LET suspension loses nothing by being forced (\code{\verb~|CONV~} forces a suspension before it looks at flags; \code{\verb~|OPEN~}-ness matters for arguments inside a spine only)}}
\tr{\td{D5}\td{11 "v0: every non-leaf node tabled"}\td{Lambda and Pi nodes have no tabling record in \code{\verb~|EVAL~}: their value is the closure, whose interning is the memo (class p: no tick, no event). Application, let and projection nodes are tabled}\td{a SUSP record per binder node would double the probes for nothing; \code{\verb~|INFER~} (M5) keeps its own record for a lambda node}}
\tr{\td{D6}\td{4.2 \code{\verb~|EVAL~} app / 4.3.1 \code{\verb~|APPLY~}}\td{\code{\verb~|EVAL~} forces the head \strong{before} it builds the arguments (\code{\verb~|EVAL[HEAD]~}, \code{\verb~|EVAL[HEADF]~}), and an argument whose binder the forced closure does not read is not built at all: its scratch slot is HOLE. \code{\verb~|APPLY~} then substitutes HOLE for unread binders again (for callers that pass values)}\td{decision 8 "never evaluated when the callee's binder is unread", 4.1 \code{\verb~|BUNREAD~}, B6. Same values; fewer suspensions made. Only the first group of leading lambdas is known before the arguments are built; later groups get built arguments and HOLE in \code{\verb~|APPLY~}}}
\tr{\td{D7}\td{13.7 "ARGV has a frame op of its own"}\td{\code{\verb~|ARGV~} never ticks and never becomes a frame: atoms and \code{\verb~|MKSUSP~} are inline, and its one sub-judgment is \code{\verb~|evalIn~}, whose frame is \code{\verb~|EVAL[IN]~}. \code{\verb~|K_ARGV~} has its \code{\verb~|resume~} case and is never written}\td{under H a judgment without work of its own before its only tail call needs no frame}}
\tr{\td{D8}\td{4.2 "variable -> GET"}\td{\code{\verb~|PEEK(GET)~}}\td{ISA 2.1 "a SUSP whose value is known is never stored where its value could be stored (PEEK, 4.2)": a variable's value is copied into spines and registers. \strong{Consequence for M7 / tier equivalence}: operands of modes R / A / C must be \code{\verb~|PEEK~}ed when they enter a spine or a frame, or K0 = K1 holds only up to \code{\verb~|PEEK~}}}
\tr{\td{D9}\td{4.2 \code{\verb~|let~}: "env = PUSH(env, MKSUSP(value, env, LET)) ... always a SUSP (2.8)"; 2.8 "\code{\verb~|let~} never creates a variable: the bound value is always a SUSP with flag LET"; 3.4 "let -> MKSUSP(value, LET) always"}\td{\strong{EVAL's let is zeta by sharing without the LET flag}: the bound value is what the argument of a beta step is (\code{\verb~|ARGV~}): an atom, an inert application built at once (frame \code{\verb~|EVAL[LET]~}), or a \em{plain} suspension of an active term; an unread let variable gets HOLE (B6). LET suspensions are made by INFER only (M5: the let variable of \code{\verb~|infer_let~}); EVAL keeps them when it meets them (\code{\verb~|PEEK~})}\td{\strong{The ISA's rule is wrong for evaluation and costs a factor of 1000 on Cedar.} Officially a let variable is a free variable only inside \code{\verb~|infer_let~} (R02 6.6; \code{\verb~|perf/let-fold~} is that case); \code{\verb~|whnf_core~} reduces a \code{\verb~|let~} of a term it evaluates by \code{\verb~|instantiate(body, value)~} (R02 7.1): no variable, no \code{\verb~|hasFVar~}. Flagging the lets of unfolded definition bodies made every value built from them OPEN, which switches off the Nat literal folding of lazy delta (R02 8.4) and the \code{\verb~|Bool.true~} shortcut (8.1 step 2); the machine then unfolded \code{\verb~|Nat.div~} / \code{\verb~|Nat.mod~} / \code{\verb~|gcd~} on literals near 2^63 by their fuel recursion. Measured on \code{\verb~|cedar-hot-ax~} unit 7008 (\code{\verb~|BitVec.neg_toInt_eq_neg_64._proof_1_1~}, an \code{\verb~|omega~} certificate whose definitions bind \code{\verb~|let~}s): 73.7 M ticks and E_MEM before, \strong{60,569 ticks and 38 ms after} (reference engine: 42 ms). ISA 2.3 allowed OPEN to over-approximate because it "only steers" those guards; it steers them into non-termination. To be applied to K1 as well (M7: \code{\verb~|MKSUSP .. LET~} in BODY / RULE blocks)}}
\tr{\td{D10}\td{4.3.1 \code{\verb~|APPLY~}: neutral -> \code{\verb~|MKAPP~}}\td{\code{\verb~|fault(E_HOLE)~} if a HOLE is among the arguments that go into the spine; \code{\verb~|APPLY~} of HOLE itself is \code{\verb~|fault(E_HOLE)~}, of any other non-function \code{\verb~|fault(E_ILLTYPED)~}}\td{a HOLE inside a NEU could be compared and found "identical"; fail closed}}
\tr{\td{D11}\td{4.3 \code{\verb~|INST~}}\td{(a) the result is \code{\verb~|PEEK~}ed and may be a suspension; \code{\verb~|COD~} is written only for a value. (b) a PII whose lambda body does not read its variable also gets HOLE and \code{\verb~|COD~} (ISA writes \code{\verb~|PUSH(frame, x)~} for PII; 2.6 lists \code{\verb~|COD~} for PI and PII). (c) \code{\verb~|INST~} / \code{\verb~|DOM~} of a record of another kind: \code{\verb~|fault(E_INTERNAL)~}}\td{(a) D1; (b) the type of a body that does not mention the variable cannot depend on it; (c) fail closed}}
\tr{\td{D12}\td{8.2 "inert evaluation is one EVAL frame looping over scratch"; \code{\verb~|Op.SW_INERT_LOOP~}}\td{\strong{Wave 6: the loop over scratch is removed; \code{\verb~|SW_INERT_LOOP~} selects nothing} (the nest runs by host recursion, beyond the depth bound as the frame \code{\verb~|EVAL[IN]~}; the 913,500-element list literal and the 1,000,000-deep nests of \code{\verb~|M2DeepTest~} pass on a 512 KiB stack under D = 64 and 0). It was measured twice as not faster (section 5), and every change of the tabling gate had to be written twice. Before: two implementations of the inert-nest loop with \strong{identical observables} (records and runs word by word, memo words, ticks, call events): default = host recursion (\code{\verb~|evalIn~}; beyond the depth bound the frame \code{\verb~|EVAL[IN]~}), \code{\verb~|SW_INERT_LOOP~} = one loop over scratch (\code{\verb~|inertLoop~}). In both the nested inert applications cost a tick each and are not call events}\td{skeleton note "behind SW_INERT_LOOP only if results stay identical"; convention H8 item 3 leaves the choice to a per-platform measurement. \code{\verb~|M2EquivTest~} compares the two word by word}}
\tr{\td{D13}\td{H4 \code{\verb~|spillN~}}\td{\code{\verb~|EVAL[IN]~} is written with \code{\verb~|m.fuel++; m.sig4(Op.SUSP, K_EVAL_IN, ..)~} instead of \code{\verb~|spill4~}}\td{\code{\verb~|spillN~} also takes back a call event, and an inner inert evaluation has none}}
\tr{\td{D14}\td{3.1 \code{\verb~|tabled(t)~} (\code{\verb~|SW_GATED_TABLING~}, step 1, off)}\td{(\code{\verb~|Eval.gate~}; with the depth rule of D21.) SHARED / BODY / INVARIANT, or an export id below the unit's first one, or a generated id. Overlay nodes go by their flags only (the decoded block of \em{another} unit's theorem is not recognised as foreign). \strong{In addition a flat inert application} (constant head; every argument a variable, constant, sort or literal) \strong{is never tabled} under the switch, whatever its flags}\td{(a) the machine cannot tell whose block an overlay node belongs to; hash-consed overlay nodes are SHARED and decoded blocks carry their segment's flags, so sharing is never under-approximated. (b) evaluating a flat application is one \code{\verb~|MKAPP~} of atoms: cheaper than its tabling probe (\code{\verb~|PRUNE~} + SUSP probe; on a miss a frame run and a 32-byte record), and there is no sub-term whose walk a memo could save, so no DAG is walked as a tree. On Init through the launcher: 10\% fewer records and 7\% fewer run words than gating by flags alone, 5\% more ticks (re-evaluations are ticks); CPU time could not be measured (host load 170+)}}
\tr{\td{D15}\td{2.4 mask bit 63}\td{A binder whose de Bruijn index in the body is 63 or more counts as read when bit 63 of the body's mask is set (no HOLE)}\td{bits 0..62 are per index; bit 63 only says "some index >= 63"}}
\tr{\td{D16}\td{5.5 \code{\verb~|memocheck~}}\td{\code{\verb~|VAL~} (at \code{\verb~|FORCE~} and at every tabled \code{\verb~|EVAL~} hit) and \code{\verb~|COD~} are checked \strong{up to PEEK}: \code{\verb~|Eval.checkVal~} / \code{\verb~|checkCod~} re-compute with the entry bypassed and accept a result that \code{\verb~|Eval.samePeekedSlow~} finds structurally equal with known \code{\verb~|VAL~}s followed; \code{\verb~|M_DOM~} uses M6's one-line check (id-stable). A LET suspension's \code{\verb~|VAL~} is not checked separately (it is the plain record's)}\td{the re-evaluation meets suspensions whose value became known after the entry was written (\code{\verb~|PEEK~}, \code{\verb~|MKSUSP~} "known VAL") and builds \code{\verb~|NEU(c, [VAL a])~} where the first run built \code{\verb~|NEU(c, [SUSP a])~}: the same value, another id. Test \code{\verb~|M2EquivTest.aMemoCheckOfValIsUpToPeek~}}}
\tr{\td{D17}\td{2.6 / 4.3.1 \code{\verb~|CODE~}}\td{Staging step 4, behind \code{\verb~|SW_CODE~} (off in v0): \code{\verb~|APPLY~} of a LAM closure and \code{\verb~|INST~} of a PI closure look the block of the binder term up once (\code{\verb~|Code.closureBlock~}, memo word \code{\verb~|CODE~}, \code{\verb~|NOCODE~} if none) and call \code{\verb~|Code.callClosure~} for \code{\verb~|j = min(leading lambdas, arguments, arity of the block)~} binders if the block has that entry; frame \code{\verb~|INST[2](memo, xb)~} for the scratch word of the argument. With the switch off the memo word is never read or written}\td{M7's request of 08:58Z; tested on M7's sub-blocks of \code{\verb~|Nat.add~} and of two Pi-making definitions (\code{\verb~|M2CodeTest~}: same value ids as the walk, call trace \code{\verb~|APPLY, ACT~} / \code{\verb~|INST, ACT~}, under D = 64 and 0)}}
\tr{\td{D18}\td{results that are no value}\td{\code{\verb~|EVAL~} / \code{\verb~|FORCE~} raise \code{\verb~|fault(E_HOLE)~} / \code{\verb~|fault(E_INTERNAL)~} when a result is HOLE / NONE (a field of a constructor application that some caller built with a HOLE) instead of storing it in \code{\verb~|VAL~}}\td{fail closed}}
\tr{\td{D19}\td{3.1 \code{\verb~|tabled(t)~}: "BODY(t): body of a binder"; 5.1 (\code{\verb~|SW_M2A~}, off)}\td{\strong{The body of a beta step (\code{\verb~|APPLY~}) and of \code{\verb~|INST~} of a PI closure is evaluated without a tabling record}, whatever its flags (\code{\verb~|evalNT~}, frame \code{\verb~|EVAL[NB]~}). The body's own inert arguments keep the gate of D14}\td{A body is entered once per \code{\verb~|APPLY~} / \code{\verb~|INST~}: its key \code{\verb~|SUSP(body, PRUNE(frame + arguments))~} is new for every new argument tuple, so the probe is a \code{\verb~|PRUNE~}, a frame run and a 32-byte record for a memo that is asked again only when the same closure meets the same read arguments (measured hit rate at this site, step 1: Init 16 \%, Cedar slice 23 \%, reachability 0.8 \%; two thirds of Init's hits are projection bodies, which cost less than the probe). It was 39 \% of all tabling probes on Init, 30 \% on the Cedar slice and \strong{81 \% on reachability}. No DAG is walked as a tree by this: \code{\verb~|EVAL~} descends strictly only into the head, the struct of a projection, a let body and the inert arguments of an inert application; a body is reached through \code{\verb~|APPLY~} (one per application node evaluated, per forced suspension, per reduction step of a value, each of which is memoised by identity), never through the fan-out of an inert nest, so the number of body evaluations is bounded by the number of beta steps, with and without the record}}
\tr{\td{D20}\td{4.2 \code{\verb~|KVAL~} "closed-term cache"; 5.1 (no switch: no result changes)}\td{\strong{Closed-term memo} \code{\verb~|Ext.cm~}: 4,096 cells \code{\verb~|(term, epoch, value)~} direct-mapped by the term id, read by the inline part of \code{\verb~|EVAL~} / \code{\verb~|ARGV~} for a closed application, let or projection under ls' = 0 (no level parameter, or the identity substitution) and written where \code{\verb~|VAL~} is written (\code{\verb~|done~}). Where the node is tabled the entry is a copy of \code{\verb~|VAL(SUSP(t, EMPTY, 0))~}: the memo saves the probe and changes no id, record, run or tick (\code{\verb~|M2EconomyTest.theClosedMemoChangesNothing~}). Where the node is not tabled (gated: flat applications, untabled nests) it is the only memo, and saves the evaluation. Bypassed under the debug modes that own a memo hit or a variable read}\td{the task's "direct-mapped memo indexed by term id for closed terms under the identity level substitution"; closed nodes are 11 \% (Init) to 17 \% (Cedar slice) of the tabling probes of v0, 80-94 \% of them hits}}
\tr{\td{D21}\td{3.1 "the test must never under-approximate sharing" (\code{\verb~|SW_GATED_TABLING~})}\td{\strong{Depth rule}: an inert application that lies \code{\verb~|depthK~} = 4 or more inert levels below the root of its nest is tabled whatever its flags (\code{\verb~|gate~}, argument \code{\verb~|u~}; the depth travels in \code{\verb~|X[xb - 1]~} and in \code{\verb~|EVAL[IN]~})}\td{\strong{Gating by flags alone is quadratic on an unshared dependent nest.} \code{\verb~|INFER~} evaluates the argument of every dependent application (\code{\verb~|TWALK~}: \code{\verb~|ARGV(t_i)~}), bottom-up; each of these evaluations walked the whole untabled nest below it again. Measured on \code{\verb~|c (c (.. x))~} with \code{\verb~|c : (x : T) -> G x~}, 4,000 applications under one binder (\code{\verb~|work/m2/gen/depnest.py~}; resource \code{\verb~|m2/depnest-open-300.ndjson~}): v0 44,030 ticks, \code{\verb~|gated~} as published in wave 4 \strong{8,038,031 ticks}, \code{\verb~|gated~} with the rule 60,017. \code{\verb~|sharecheck~} reports such walks (it fails on 196 units of init-prelude under \code{\verb~|gated~}, before and after this wave: an untabled node is legitimately visited once per evaluation root above it); with the rule each node is visited at most \code{\verb~|depthK~} + 1 times. On the corpora the rule costs nothing measurable (Cedar slice: +0.5 \% records, -6 \% ticks together with D20)}}
\tr{\td{D22}\td{4.3.1 \code{\verb~|APPLY~} (argument picker: no switch; projection selector: \code{\verb~|SW_M2A~})}\td{A beta step whose body is one of the variables it binds returns that argument, PEEKed (\code{\verb~|pick~}: what \code{\verb~|EVAL~} of the variable returns; HOLE is \code{\verb~|fault(E_HOLE)~}), without building the environment: no record, run or tick differs. With \code{\verb~|SW_M2A~} a body that is a projection of a bound variable is \code{\verb~|MKPROJ~} of the argument (\code{\verb~|betaProj~}): no environment, no tick, no call event of the body}\td{selector patterns of the task (item 2). Bodies at \code{\verb~|APPLY~} on Init: projection of a variable 10.6 \%, argument 3.1 \% (reachability 4.8 \% / 5.6 \%)}}
\tr{\td{D23}\td{4.3.1 \code{\verb~|APPLY~} (\code{\verb~|SW_M2B~}, off)}\td{\strong{APPLY memo} \code{\verb~|Ext.am~}: 2,048 cells \code{\verb~|(closure, a0, a1, a2, epoch, j, value)~}, direct-mapped and lossy, for a beta step of j <= 3 binders whose body is not a binder; the key holds the arguments as \code{\verb~|bind~} binds them (HOLE for a binder the body does not read), so it is the key of the body's tabling record without the \code{\verb~|PRUNE~}. Written when the step completes (frame \code{\verb~|APPLY[3]~} on the worklist path, so D = 0 and D = 64 fill it alike). \strong{Governor} (\code{\verb~|amLive~}): after a window of 4,096 lookups with fewer than 256 hits the memo is passed by for 65,536 beta steps, then tried again (a function of the session's history only)}\td{gives back the memo that D19 removes, for 2 probes of 32 bytes instead of a \code{\verb~|PRUNE~} and two records: repeated steps are 17 \% (Init), 23 \% (Cedar slice), 1.2 \% (reachability) of all beta steps}}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{3. Why the two inert-nest implementations were the same machine (historic: the loop was removed in wave 6, D12)}

\p{Per node of a nest both do, in this order: tabling probe (\code{\verb~|PRUNE~}, SUSP record; hit: the value), tick, spine into scratch, head value (\code{\verb~|KCONST~}, or the variable's neutral), the arguments left to right (atom / \code{\verb~|MKSUSP~} of an active term / the nested inert application, recursively), \code{\verb~|MKAPP~}, \code{\verb~|VAL := result~}. Records and runs are appended in that order, so the session arrays are equal word by word. Scratch layout differs (recursion: the arguments only; loop: a 5-word header \code{\verb~|[prev, s, f, n, i]~} per node) and is not observable.}
}

\subtree{
\title{4. Open points}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Gated tabling} (D14, D21) is gated on all 230 tests and the four corpora (section 6). \strong{\code{\verb~|sharecheck~} is not a gate for it}: the hook reports every second visit of an untabled node under one frame in a declaration, and such visits are legitimate (an evaluation root above the node, a second application of an untabled body under \code{\verb~|m2a~}); it fails on 196 units of init-prelude under \code{\verb~|gated~}. A version that counts visits per evaluation root would need an activation serial in the audit's key (M6's \code{\verb~|Debug.shareCheck~}); not done.}
\li{\strong{What \code{\verb~|m2a~} gives up}: a second application of one closure to the same read arguments evaluates the body again (\code{\verb~|m2b~} gives most of it back). The number of body evaluations is bounded by the number of beta steps (D19), so no walk becomes exponential; the perf/ tests need at most 1.12 times the ticks (section 6).}
\li{\strong{Unread arguments of constant spines} (the facts' unread masks; task item 2) are not used: an argument of a NEU is part of its identity and of its type, so leaving it out needs the fact "neither the body nor the type telescope reads it" (M5's fact records, \code{\verb~|SW_FACTS~}) and a HOLE-aware \code{\verb~|CARGS~}; nothing of it is in this file.}
\li{\strong{\code{\verb~|K_ARGV~}} stays in \code{\verb~|Op~} and in the \code{\verb~|resume~} switch although no such frame is written (D7).}
\li{\strong{Callers and suspensions}: \code{\verb~|Infer~} opens binders with \code{\verb~|OPEN(EVAL(A))~}, which may be a suspension, while \code{\verb~|CBIND~} / \code{\verb~|ETA~} use \code{\verb~|DOM~} (forced): the same binder can get two different variables (never a wrong answer; advice sent to M5).}
\li{\strong{Tier equivalence} (M7 / M8, step 4): K1 operands must be \code{\verb~|PEEK~}ed where K0 does (D8), or the comparison is up to \code{\verb~|PEEK~} (\code{\verb~|Eval.samePeekedSlow~} is that relation).}
\li{The depth of \code{\verb~|samePeekedSlow~} is 24; beyond it a memo check is inconclusive (accepted).}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{5. Measurements (not gates)}

\p{Host: the project machine (aarch64, 20 cores), \strong{shared with 15 other agents running builds and tests}, JVM with the Graal JIT (\code{\verb~|-Xss2m -Xmx6g -XX:+UseSerialGC~}, the module's surefire settings), no Docker, no arena limits. CPU time of the worker thread (\code{\verb~|ThreadMXBean~}), minimum over the timed rounds after one warm-up round. Run-to-run spread on this host was 10-15\%, so differences below that are not established.}

\p{\code{\verb~|M2PerfTest~} on \code{\verb~|work/exports/init.ndjson~} (59,979 constants): for every constant \code{\verb~|EVAL(type)~} and the walk of its Pi telescope (\code{\verb~|DOM~}, \code{\verb~|OPEN~}, \code{\verb~|INST~}, \code{\verb~|FORCE~} per binder); for every definition \code{\verb~|EVAL(value)~} and the walk of its lambda telescope (\code{\verb~|DOM~}, \code{\verb~|OPEN~}, \code{\verb~|APPLY~}); then every suspension reachable from the body's value is forced. Sessions reset at 16 MiB. No environment pass (so no projection-of-constructor and no \code{\verb~|Nat.succ~} folding in this run).}

\table{
\tr{\th{Configuration}\th{CPU time}\th{Ticks}\th{Frames written (per call event)}\th{Records / run words made}}
\tr{\td{D = 64 (v0 default)}\td{180 ms}\td{746,071}\td{198 (0.00032)}\td{716,442 / 1,809,042}}
\tr{\td{D = unbounded}\td{202 ms}\td{746,071}\td{0}\td{the same}}
\tr{\td{D = 64, \code{\verb~|SW_INERT_LOOP~}}\td{192 ms}\td{746,071}\td{0}\td{the same}}
\tr{\td{D = 0 (worklist machine)}\td{224 ms}\td{746,071}\td{392,894 (0.63)}\td{the same}}
\tr{\td{D = 64, \code{\verb~|SW_GATED_TABLING~}}\td{177 ms}\td{754,647}\td{198}\td{677,864 / 1,770,339}}
\tr{\td{D = 64, gated + inert loop}\td{189 ms}\td{754,647}\td{0}\td{the same}}
}

\p{A first run without the forcing phase gave 160 / 158 / 165 / 186 / 181 / 166 ms for the same six rows (742,097 ticks). Call events in the D = 64 row: EVAL 78,767, FORCE 1,293, APPLY 55,465, INST 227,922, DOM 260,799; tabled-EVAL hits 206,273; 291,748 binders opened; 730,028 values visited by the forcing phase, of which 1,293 were pending suspensions.}

\p{Readings: (1) about 240 ns of CPU per tick including session resets, \code{\verb~|OPEN~} / \code{\verb~|CLOSE~} and 716 k new records (at the 55 ns per new record of ISA 0.3 that alone is 40 ms); (2) frames written per call event at D = 64 are 0.03\%, below the 0.1\% bound of convention H12; (3) D = 0 costs about +25\% on this workload, D = 64 against unbounded is inside the noise; (4) the inert-nest loop is not faster than bounded recursion here (inside the noise), as the stepper spike found, so it stays off; (5) on Init's types and definition bodies under variables almost every argument is an atom or inert: 1,293 pending suspensions among 730 k values; (6) gated tabling saves 5\% of the records on this workload (its nodes are mostly foreign to the unit under evaluation or flagged).}

\p{The whole machine on Init through the launcher (\code{\verb~|work/dist/bin/rlvm-jvm -X engine=machine --threads 1 work/exports/init.ndjson~}, HotSpot C2, published jar of 09:09Z, v0: a session per declaration): 57,938 declarations accepted, 0 declined; 93.57 M ticks, 79.17 M call events, of which \strong{46.5 M (59\%) are family EV}: EVAL 13.69 M, INST 13.51 M, APPLY 11.89 M, DOM 6.93 M, FORCE 0.55 M. 54.68 M records and 241.4 M run words were made. Worker CPU time 12.7 s in the quietest run (host load about 100) and 16-20 s later (load 170-190): not a usable number, only an order of magnitude (reference engine 54 s, gruszka 2.8 s). A JFR profile of that run (441 samples of the worker thread; self time): \code{\verb~|PRUNE~} 21\% (\code{\verb~|Runs.pruneSlow~} 12\%, \code{\verb~|pruneNear~} 8\%), \code{\verb~|Machine.addRecordAt~} 12.5\%, \code{\verb~|Values.rec~} 7.5\%, \code{\verb~|Eval.eval~} + \code{\verb~|atom~} + \code{\verb~|node~} + \code{\verb~|app~} 17\%, \code{\verb~|Values.neu~} 4.5\%, \code{\verb~|Machine.reset~} 3.6\%. About two thirds of the \code{\verb~|PRUNE~} time is under \code{\verb~|Eval.table~} (the tabling probe of every application, let and projection node), the rest under closure construction.}

\p{Tabling variants on the same run (records / run words / ticks; all 57,938 accepted):}

\table{
\tr{\th{Switches}\th{Records}\th{Run words}\th{Ticks}}
\tr{\td{none (v0: every node tabled)}\td{54.68 M}\td{241.4 M}\td{93.57 M}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|gated~} by the node flags alone (before D14's flat rule)}\td{53.34 M}\td{239.6 M}\td{93.96 M}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|gated~} with the flat rule (published)}\td{48.17 M}\td{222.3 M}\td{98.38 M}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|inert~}}\td{54.68 M}\td{241.4 M}\td{93.57 M (frames written 168,809 instead of 185,128)}}
}

\p{Reading: the node flags alone gate little on Init because most evaluated nodes are foreign to the unit being checked (types and bodies of earlier constants); what remains to be saved is in the \code{\verb~|PRUNE~} itself (M1: dense frames, the OPEN-bit loads) and in sessions that survive a declaration (M6, step 1).}

\p{\strong{Cedar level} (owner note 9): \code{\verb~|work/workloads/slices/cedar-hot-ax.ndjson~} through the launcher (\code{\verb~|-X engine=machine --threads 1~}, v0 switches, C2, host load about 130), before and after the let fix of D9:}

\table{
\tr{\th{Jar}\th{Machine accepted / declined}\th{Worker CPU}\th{Ticks}\th{Records}\th{Run words}\th{Reference re-checks}}
\tr{\td{09:59Z (every let value a LET suspension, as ISA 2.8 / 4.2 say)}\td{8,059 / 10 (E_MEM)}\td{168 s}\td{786 M}\td{554 M}\td{2.9 G}\td{5 units, 348,591 steps}}
\tr{\td{10:26Z (EVAL's let = zeta by sharing, plain values)}\td{\strong{8,064 / 0}}\td{\strong{4.63 s}}\td{18.1 M}\td{10.4 M}\td{103 M}\td{0}}
}

\p{For scale: nano-lean 3.4 s, the official checker 20 s on this slice (R13 section 6). Five \code{\verb~|omega~} certificates carried the first row: each ran 73.7 M ticks into E_MEM where the reference engine needs about 70,000 steps. After the fix the call events are INFER 1.77 M, CONV 1.38 M, CBIND 0.97 M, EVAL 2.41 M (hit rate 66\%), APPLY 2.26 M, INST 1.98 M, DOM 2.57 M, DELTA 0.52 M, LSTEP 0.32 M.}

\p{\code{\verb~|work/exports/reachability.ndjson~} (closed evaluation) with the same jar and settings: 4,224 engine checks accepted, 0 declined; worker CPU 7.3 s; 34.6 M ticks; EVAL 8.35 M, APPLY 8.20 M, FORCE 0.51 M, INST 0.13 M, DOM 0.17 M; 22.9 M records, 138 M run words, 356,561 frames written.}

\p{Stack safety (\code{\verb~|M2DeepTest~}, group \code{\verb~|slow~}, 38 s for all five): a 913,500-element list literal (913,501 ticks, one call event), 1,000,000-deep application, binder and mixed nests and a 1,000,000-long chain of suspensions, each on a 512 KiB thread stack under D = 64 and D = 0, with and without the inert loop: identical value ids, records, runs and ticks in the four configurations.}
}

