}

\subtree{
\title{Final A/B of the published code}

\p{base = the main tree of 15:26Z with the wave-5 \code{\verb~|Eval~} (\code{\verb~|work/m2/base2~}, image \code{\verb~|work/m2/dist-base2n~}); new = the same tree with \code{\verb~|Eval~} as published at 15:26Z (\code{\verb~|work/m2/dist-r5n~}; the entry \code{\verb~|evalBody~} of 15:34Z is not called by anything measured). Both trees hold the other packages' work of this wave, among it M6's eager-reduction rule: 11 / 8 / 164 / 203 units of the Cedar slice / reachability / Init / Std are declined by design and checked by the reference engine in every row.}

