\p{Peak RSS, step 1 -> step 1 + \code{\verb~|m2a~}: Cedar slice 182 -> 176 MiB, reachability 1,136 -> 774 MiB, Init 246 -> 214 MiB, Std 366 -> 372 MiB. The v0 row of the Cedar slice (+2.3 \%) is two readings of 2.95 and 2.77 s against 2.83 and 2.76 s with 0.7 \% fewer instructions: noise of that pass, not a cost (the second pass is equal).}

\p{Reading: \strong{\code{\verb~|gated~} with the depth rule and \code{\verb~|m2a~} are ready}: every corpus is faster in CPU time (10 \% to 38 \% against step 1) and none is slower. \strong{\code{\verb~|m2b~} is not decided}: it lowers the Cedar slice (instructions -1.8 \%, CPU -3 \% in means of two noisy readings) and Init / Std by 0.5 \% of the instructions, and raises reachability by 0.4 \% of the instructions and by 2.3 \% of the CPU time in the rows with statistics (0.2 \% in the row without): inside the noise, but above the 1 \% rule on the face of the numbers. It stays off.}

\p{Against the yardstick (gruszka on this host: Init 2.63 s, Std 5.62 s, Cedar slice 1.91 s, reachability 3.97 s): step 1 + \code{\verb~|m2a~} is at 6.35 / 11.87 / 2.72 / 4.94 s (2.41x / 2.11x / 1.42x / 1.24x).}

\p{Gates of the published code (jar of 15:34Z, \code{\verb~|work/m2/dist-r6p~}; \code{\verb~|testkit diff --engine machine~} through the launcher, reports in \code{\verb~|work/m2/diff/~}): tutorial + bugs (1,342 units) with v0, step 1 + \code{\verb~|m2a~}, step 1 + \code{\verb~|m2a,m2b~} and \code{\verb~|gated,m2a,m2b~} at hostDepth 0: 0 differences, 0 declines. All 230 tests with each of v0, step 1 + \code{\verb~|m2a~}, step 1 + \code{\verb~|m2a,m2b~}: 0 differences; 15,839 of 15,845 units compared in each run (the four memory-hungry perf files in a run of their own with a 10 GiB heap), not compared: five units that M6's eager-reduction rule declines by design and \code{\verb~|loop_unfolded_once~} (E_MEM, as before this wave without M4's former B12 probe). Four corpora with each of the three configurations: Cedar slice 8,053 of 8,064, reachability 4,216 of 4,224, Init 57,774 of 57,938, Std 99,893 of 100,096 units compared, all agree, 0 differences; the units not compared are the eager-reduction declines (11 / 8 / 164 / 203). On the code of 15:10Z, before that rule arrived in the tree, the same four corpora with v0 and step 1 + \code{\verb~|m2a~}: every unit compared, 0 differences, 0 declines.}

