\p{Four workers cost the CPU of one (Init 6.46 against 6.35 s), and peak RSS falls with the records (reachability 2,191-2,498 -> 1,437-1,637 MiB). The wall clock of a loaded host scatters by a factor of two between passes; the medians are lower with \code{\verb~|m2a~} on every corpus.}

\p{After these batches: the request of M1 (16:48:45Z: \code{\verb~|Eval.closure~} / \code{\verb~|table~} / \code{\verb~|suspend~} call M1's combined constructors \code{\verb~|Values.mkLamAt~} / \code{\verb~|mkPiAt~} / \code{\verb~|suspRecordAt~} / \code{\verb~|mkSuspAt~}; the same frames, records and ids; M1 measured reachability v0 8.29 -> 7.69 s with it) and M5's use of \code{\verb~|Eval.evalBody~} in \code{\verb~|TWALK~} (16:03Z). Gates of that jar (\code{\verb~|work/m2/dist-r8p~}): tutorial + bugs with v0, step 1 + \code{\verb~|m2a~} and \code{\verb~|gated,m2a,m2b~} at hostDepth 0, the four corpora with v0 and with step 1 + \code{\verb~|m2a~}, all 230 with step 1 + \code{\verb~|m2a~}: 0 differences (not compared: the eager-reduction declines and \code{\verb~|loop_unfolded_once~}, as above). Instructions of that tree (\code{\verb~|work/m2/dist-r8n~}, unlocked, one run): the machine's default switch set is \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~} since about 16:00Z (M6) and has a session cap of its own, which doubles the resets on Init (1,129 -> 2,160) and raises the ticks of every warm configuration by 20 \% (54.95 M -> 66.11 M; \code{\verb~|-X machine.session-kib=0~} gives the old figure): Init default 116.4 G, default + \code{\verb~|m2a~} 106.2 G (-8.8 \%); step 1 + \code{\verb~|m2a~}: Cedar slice 38.8 G, reachability 48.0 G, Init 108.0 G, Std 186.3 G.}
